From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: apklayer <apklayer@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ShadowUserManager: getAliveUsers, getUserProperties

apklayer patch: getAliveUsers() returns the users that exist (the settings provider migrates its settings for each at start);
getUserProperties(UserHandle) returns a full user's default UserProperties (the fake user service has none; DocumentsUI reads it).

Against external/robolectric 87aa52b08 (REVISION). Applied by scripts/build-runtime-overlay.sh onto the staged
upstream sources (<native>/aosp/robolectric-src); the result is compiled into native-runtime.jar ahead of Robolectric_all.jar.
---
diff --git a/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowUserManager.java b/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowUserManager.java
--- a/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowUserManager.java
+++ b/shadows/framework/src/main/java/org/robolectric/shadows/ShadowUserManager.java
@@ -201,6 +201,18 @@
   public long addUserProfile(UserHandle userHandle) {
     addProfile(UserHandle.myUserId(), userHandle.getIdentifier(), "", 0);
     return userManagerState.userSerialNumbers.get(userHandle.getIdentifier());
+  }
+
+  // apklayer patch: the users that exist (the settings provider migrates its settings for each of them at start)
+  @Implementation
+  protected List<UserInfo> getAliveUsers() {
+    return new ArrayList<>(userManagerState.userInfoMap.values());
+  }
+
+  // apklayer patch: UserManager.getUserProperties() answers the properties of a full user (the fake user service has none, apps read a profile's properties)
+  @Implementation(minSdk = UPSIDE_DOWN_CAKE)
+  protected android.content.pm.UserProperties getUserProperties(UserHandle userHandle) {
+    return new android.content.pm.UserProperties.Builder().build();
   }
 
   @Implementation
